  "identifier": "pannuke",
  "name": "PanNuke",
  "description": "Pan-cancer nucleus instance segmentation and classification dataset covering ~200,000 nuclei across 5 clinically important classes (neoplastic, non-neoplastic epithelial, inflammatory, connective, dead) and 19 tissue types — the broadest tissue coverage of any public nucleus segmentation dataset. Organised into three cross-validation folds. Used as the primary training and evaluation benchmark for HoVer-Net, CellViT, and most nucleus classification models. Published by the Tissue Image Analytics (TIA) Centre, University of Warwick (Gamper et al. 2019 + 2020). CC-BY-NC-SA-4.0, available from the TIA Centre website.",
  "url": "https://warwick.ac.uk/fac/cross_fac/tia/data/pannuke",
  "relatedLink": [
    "https://arxiv.org/abs/2003.10778"
  ],
  "license": "CC-BY-NC-SA-4.0",
  "keywords": [
